---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { siteFromHost } from '../../content';

const site = siteFromHost();
const path = '/compare/klaviyo-vs-privy';
const title = "Klaviyo vs Privy for Shopify email: 2026 comparison";
const desc = "For an existing Privy merchant, the immediate question is continuity and capture handoff; new installations need availability confirmation.";
const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "Can I install Privy from Shopify today?",
    "answer": "The listing checked November 24, 2026 says it is unavailable. Confirm current access with the supplier before planning installation."
  },
  {
    "question": "Does Klaviyo require a separate popup app?",
    "answer": "Its listing includes sign-up forms. Compare your actual display, offer and consent requirements before adding another app."
  },
  {
    "question": "Should an existing Privy user immediately disconnect?",
    "answer": "The listing does not establish existing-account continuity. Confirm service and exports, then verify a replacement before cutover."
  }
];
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
  <section class="py-14 md:py-20">
    <div class="container">
      <nav class="mb-8 text-sm"><a class="link" href="/compare">Comparisons</a></nav>
      <header class="max-w-4xl">
        <p class="editorial-kicker">Head-to-head</p>
        <h1 class="hero-title mt-5">Klaviyo vs Privy for Shopify email</h1>
        <p class="mt-7 max-w-3xl text-xl leading-9 text-[#4a2d17]">For an existing Privy merchant, the immediate question is continuity and capture handoff; new installations need availability confirmation.</p>
      </header>
      <article class="prose-shopify mt-14 max-w-4xl">
        <h2>Availability comes before the feature comparison</h2>
        <p>The <a href="https://apps.shopify.com/privy">Privy Shopify listing</a> says the app is not currently available and directs support questions to Privy Operations, as checked November 24, 2026. That does not establish why it is unavailable, whether an existing account will continue operating, or when availability might change. Confirm those points directly before committing to an installation or migration timetable.</p>
        <h2>What Klaviyo currently offers</h2>
        <p>The <a href="https://apps.shopify.com/klaviyo-email-marketing">Klaviyo listing</a> advertises sign-up forms, a welcome email, abandoned-checkout setup, segmentation and automated workflows. This contradicts the idea that capture must always live outside Klaviyo. It does not prove that its forms reproduce every display rule, design or offer in an existing Privy installation.</p>
        <h2>Inventory the existing capture experience</h2>
        <p>For each active form, record where it appears, mobile behavior, audience targeting, frequency rules, offer text, coupon source, destination list and any follow-up email. Include embedded forms and landing pages that are easy to miss. Capture screenshots and settings from your own account. An export of email addresses alone cannot reconstruct this experience.</p>
        <h2>Proposed handoff exercise: a returning subscriber</h2>
        <p>This exercise has not been run. Use a test identity that previously subscribed, then revisit a collection page and submit the replacement form. Inspect whether the original permission history remains, whether the signup source is updated intentionally, and whether another welcome discount is sent. Repeat with a new subscriber and a visitor who declines permission. Keep test messages isolated from real shoppers.</p>
        <h2>Choose a single coupon-delivery owner</h2>
        <p>If a form displays a code onsite and also triggers a welcome message, define whether both are intentional. Check code expiry, eligibility, reuse and purchase suppression. During migration, disable the old follow-up before enabling the new one. Otherwise a correct data sync can still produce two offers because two independent automations respond to the same signup.</p>
        <h2>Separate capture quality from raw signup count</h2>
        <p>Compare form exposure, valid opt-ins and subsequent engagement by device and acquisition source. An aggressive offer may increase addresses while attracting discount-only signups. Use the same denominator and observation window when comparing forms. There is no universal capture-rate percentage in this page that proves a platform is needed or that a store must migrate.</p>
        <h2>Audit email journeys independently</h2>
        <p>If the existing account sends email, inventory welcome, cart, post-purchase and winback logic rather than assuming they are all simple. Rebuild the actual branches, exclusions, product blocks and re-entry rules in the candidate tool. Identify specific missing requirements. A flat repeat-purchase rate alone cannot diagnose a software limitation; product replenishment, acquisition mix and offer strategy can also matter.</p>
        <h2>Continuity and cost worksheet</h2>
        <p>Ask Privy support about existing-account service, export access, billing, forms and connected data destinations. Ask the replacement vendor for a quote covering the intended audience, message calendar and form requirements. Include rebuilding creative, redirecting integrations and staff training. Keep the current working setup until the replacement is verified and the cutover owner can disable old triggers.</p>
        <h2>Decision</h2>
        <p>For a new store, resolve installation availability before treating Privy as a deployable choice. For an existing store, compare a verified continuation plan with a tested replacement of both capture and email responsibilities. Klaviyo may consolidate those responsibilities when its forms and journeys pass the requirements. A split setup remains an option only when availability, support and a useful capture capability are confirmed.</p>
      </article>
      <div class="mt-10 max-w-4xl text-sm">
        <p class="font-black text-[#24170f]">Related comparisons</p>
        <p class="mt-2">
          <a class="link" href="/compare/omnisend-vs-privy">Omnisend vs Privy</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/compare/privy-vs-justuno">Privy vs Justuno</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/for/jewelry">Email apps for jewelry stores</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/use-cases/abandoned-cart">Abandoned cart playbook</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <FaqSection faqs={faqs} title="Klaviyo vs Privy for Shopify email FAQ" />
</BaseLayout>
